## gluonts

`tools/score_gifteval.py` and `tools/score_official_protocol.py` compute
accuracy metrics (MASE, weighted quantile loss) using gluonts's evaluation
functions (`gluonts.ev`, `gluonts.model.evaluate_model`).

- Project: https://github.com/awslabs/gluonts
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0

## GIFT-Eval

The accuracy benchmark protocol, task configs, and dataset windowing used
by the GIFT-Eval scoring tools (`tools/gifteval_subset.py`,
`tools/gifteval_official_export.py`, `fixtures/gifteval/`) come from the
GIFT-Eval benchmark.

- Project: https://github.com/SalesforceAIResearch/gift-eval
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0
- The underlying per-dataset time series (e.g. `electricity`, `solar`,
  `jena_weather`, `saugeenday`, `LOOP_SEATTLE`, `us_births`) are drawn from
  GIFT-Eval's own dataset collection, largely sourced from the Monash Time
  Series Forecasting Archive (Godahewa et al. 2021,
  https://forecastingdata.org/) and similar public research archives.
  See GIFT-Eval's own documentation for the license of each individual
  dataset; `web/data/README.md` in this repo documents the specific
  provenance and license (CC BY 4.0 / public domain) of the one series
  bundled with the browser demo (`us_births`).

## Burn / cubecl

The CPU engine (`t0-core`, native and WASM) and the native Burn `wgpu`
backend are built on the Burn deep-learning framework and its cubecl
GPU-kernel compiler. `t0-fast` uses wgpu directly
(https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu, Apache-2.0 OR MIT).

- Project: https://github.com/tracel-ai/burn and https://github.com/tracel-ai/cubecl
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0 OR MIT (dual-licensed)

## onnxruntime-web

`bench/compare/` loads onnxruntime-web at runtime from the jsdelivr CDN
to compare this port against the official ONNX export. onnxruntime-web is
not vendored or redistributed here.

- Project: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
- License: MIT

## GGUF / ggml block-quantization format

`crates/t0-core/src/gguf.rs` implements the GGUF v3 container format and
the Q8_0/Q4_0 block quantization layout as documented by the ggml/llama.cpp
project (32 values per block, f16 scale, packed int8/nibble payload). This
is an independent Rust reimplementation from the published format and
rounding conventions; no ggml/llama.cpp source code is copied. GGUF
Q8_0/Q4_0 block layout compatible with ggml/llama.cpp.

- Format reference: https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml and
  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
